    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e4beb2b3_07d07f6e",
        "filename": "common/ccd_config.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1122,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-27T15:58:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why? This is an underlying mechanism, allowing empty string here does not require changes in CCD and gives the host side more flexibility.\n\nRandall, what do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "f7e6be03_f474e521",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1122,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 1122,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "54f2f0ce80b5c5824fb54a826247ff41d373a247",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "49952df3_9ceefc86",
        "filename": "common/ccd_config.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1122,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-27T16:15:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, on the host side, it\u0027d be bad if \u0027gsctool -P\u0027 by itself cleared the password.  So we need \u0027gsctool -P clear\u0027 anyway.\n\nSo I don\u0027t see a use case for an empty string.  Or if we did want it, then we should make do_ccd_password() take the empty string and do the check for \u0027clear\u0027 in command_ccd_password().  But then we\u0027re duplicating the check for \u0027clear\u0027 there and in gsctool.\n\nSo, let\u0027s just require \u0027clear\u0027 as the magic password that means \u0027clear the password\u0027 everywhere.",
      "parentUuid": "e4beb2b3_07d07f6e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1122,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 1122,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "54f2f0ce80b5c5824fb54a826247ff41d373a247",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
